<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Filth_MouseTrack.xml   UtinniPatches — SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S4 build pass

  "Mice deposit RUT_Filth_MouseTrack (low-alpha filth, slow dissipation) on
  tar cells they cross" (sump_kit_spec.md S4, "Mouse-line telegraphy"). No
  new C# — plain FilthDef, ParentName="BaseFilth" (vanilla's own abstract
  parent, Data/Core/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Filth_Various.xml, read directly).

  🔴 Texture path corrected this pass, caught by validate_patch.py, not
  guessed around: a first draft reused vanilla's own Things/Filth/Grainy
  (Filth_Dirt/Filth_AnimalFilth's own texture) verbatim, matching this
  item's own S1/S6/S5 posture of reusing existing vanilla art as a
  placeholder — but validate_patch.py refused it as a hard ERROR, not the
  WARN that pattern got for RUT_TarBlaze/RUT_WickStem: this mod
  (UtinniPatches) already ships its own content under Textures/Things/,
  which flips the validator's heuristic from "ambiguous vanilla, can't
  tell" to "this mod's own claimed namespace, must resolve for real" — the
  SAME "validate_patch.py refuses a cross-mod vanilla-art reuse as a hard
  ERROR" shape src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt's own F2/F5/F6 hold block already
  documents for RUT_TibannaGas/RUT_DeadCreep/etc. Repointed to a new
  RUT_-named path under the same vanilla-mirroring folder
  (Things/Filth/RUT_MouseTrack) and DEPLOY_HOLD'd — same fix, same
  pattern, this item's first time hitting it. Color is
  a much lower alpha than either vanilla filth (Dirt: 91,75,65,97 / ~38%
  opaque) — (20,18,16,42), ~16% opaque — for the spec's own "low-alpha,
  faint tracery" framing: legible up close, easy to miss at a glance,
  exactly the "the player who looks sees the gap" register.

  placementMask [Terrain] (matching Filth_Dirt/Filth_AnimalFilth's own
  choice, not the "Unnatural" default most incident-caused filth uses — a
  mouse's own footprint is closer to those two than to blood/vomit/wreckage).
  ignoreFilthMultiplierStat true — NOT a fix for an engine block
  (StatDefOf.FilthMultiplier defaults to 1/100% and nothing in this chain
  overrides it, confirmed against Stats_Basics_Special.xml) but a
  deliberate choice so RM_CompFilthTrail.chancePerCellMoved is the ONLY
  density knob in the deposit path, not diluted by an unrelated per-terrain
  stat a future terrain edit could silently change — see
  RM_CompFilthTrail.cs's own header for the full filth-cap finding this
  pass made (Filth.cs's hardcoded 5-thickness cap does NOT erase the
  pattern; the real engine block found was RM_TarShallow's inherited
  filthAcceptanceMask=None, fixed by RUT_TarShallow_FilthAcceptance.xml,
  this same pass, a separate file).

  disappearsInDays 6~10 — INVENTED, this pass's own tuning value (the spec
  names no figure beyond "slow dissipation"). Vanilla's own ambient filth
  (Filth_Dirt/Filth_AnimalFilth) uses 45~50 days, but that is filth players
  actively clean or ignore for a whole colony's lifetime; a MUCH slower
  cycle here would mean the tracery essentially never redraws, so an old
  gap (from a bulge that has since re-submerged elsewhere, per owner card 3)
  could read as a false warning for weeks. 6~10 days is fast enough that the
  pattern regenerates within roughly a week of mouse traffic — fast enough
  to stay honest, still "slow" next to a single day/night cycle.
  canFilthAttach/rainWashes are both left at their FilthProperties defaults
  (false / false) — rainWashes is moot regardless, since ban #4 (S6, the
  weather lock) means the Sump never rolls rain that could wash anything.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseFilth">
    <defName>RUT_Filth_MouseTrack</defName>
    <label>mouse track</label>
    <description>A faint smear in the black — a sump-mouse's own trail, crossing the tar. Where the tracks stop, something else has been through first.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Filth/RUT_MouseTrack</texPath>
      <color>(20,18,16,42)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <filth>
      <placementMask>
        <li>Terrain</li>
      </placementMask>
      <ignoreFilthMultiplierStat>true</ignoreFilthMultiplierStat>
      <disappearsInDays>6~10</disappearsInDays>
      <cleaningWorkToReduceThickness>10</cleaningWorkToReduceThickness>
    </filth>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
